:Namespace Tester
⍝ A small test framework for Dyalog APL.  Docs: testing/README.md
⍝
⍝ Put tests in files named Something_test.aplf, either next to the code
⍝ they test or in a tests/ subfolder (then the code is loaded from the
⍝ parent folder). A test is a function with no arguments (or a dfn):
⍝
⍝     ∇ Add_test
⍝       5 ExpectEq 2 Add 3                ⍝ expected ExpectEq actual
⍝       ExpectTrue 0<Add/⍳4
⍝       5 ExpectError '1 2 Add 1 2 3'     ⍝ 5 = LENGTH ERROR (0 = any error)
⍝     ∇
⍝
⍝ Run every test under a folder (or one test file):
⍝     dyalog test [folder|file]                  from the shell
⍝     Tester.Run '/app/path'                     from a session; returns 0 or 1
⍝
⍝ Each test file runs in a fresh namespace with the folder's code loaded
⍝ (.apli, .apln, .aplc, .aplf, .aplo, and .apla files as variables).

    ⎕IO←1 ⋄ ⎕ML←1
    Skip←'node_modules' '.venv' '__pycache__'        ⍝ folders never searched
    Order←'.apli' '.apln' '.aplc' '.aplf' '.aplo'    ⍝ load order: interfaces first
    Asserts←'ExpectEq' 'ExpectTrue' 'ExpectFalse' 'ExpectNear' 'ExpectError' 'Fail' '⍙Where' '⍙Show'

    ∇ code←Run path;files;t0;res;folder;t;r;counts;secs
    ⍝ Run all *_test.aplf under path. Prints a report; returns 0 if all passed.
      t0←⎕AI[3]
      files←FindTests path
      :If 0=≢files
          ⎕←'No *_test.aplf files found in ',path
          code←0 ⋄ :Return
      :EndIf
      res←⍬
      :For folder :In ∪Folder¨files
          ⎕←'' ⋄ ⎕←folder
          :For t :In (folder∘≡¨Folder¨files)/files
              res,←⊂r←RunOne t
              Report r
          :EndFor
      :EndFor
      counts←+⌿(⊃¨res)∘.≡'pass' 'fail' 'error'
      secs←(⎕AI[3]-t0)÷1000
      ⎕←''
      ⎕←(⍕≢res),' tests: ',(⍕counts[1]),' passed, ',(⍕counts[2]),' failed, ',(⍕counts[3]),' errors  (',(⍕secs),' s)'
      code←0<+/1↓counts
    ∇

    ∇ r←RunOne file;ns;name;warn;at;call
    ⍝ Run one test file in a fresh namespace. r: status name messages checks
      ns←#.⎕NS''
      {}ns.⎕FX¨⎕NR¨Asserts               ⍝ give the sandbox the Expect… functions
      warn←ns LoadCode CodeFolder file
      ns.(⍙fails ⍙checks)←⍬ 0
      :Trap 0
          name←⊃2 ns.⎕FIX'file://',file
      :Else
          r←'error'(2⊃⎕NPARTS file)(warn,⊂'could not load the test file: ',ErrorText ⍬)0
          :Return
      :EndTrap
      at←⊃ns.⎕AT name                    ⍝ (has-result valence …)
      call←((1⊃at)/'⍙r←'),name,((0≠2⊃at)/' ⍬')
      :Trap 0
          ns⍎call
          r←((1+0=≢ns.⍙fails)⊃'fail' 'pass')name(warn,ns.⍙fails)ns.⍙checks
      :Else
          r←'error'name(warn,ns.⍙fails,⊂ErrorText ⍬)ns.⍙checks
      :EndTrap
    ∇

    ∇ warn←ns LoadCode folder;names;types;files;ext;todo;failed;f;pass
    ⍝ Load the source files in folder (not the tests) into namespace ns.
      (names types)←0 1(⎕NINFO⍠1)folder,'*'
      files←(types=2)/names
      files←files/⍨~∨/¨'_test.aplf'∘⍷¨files
      ext←{3⊃⎕NPARTS ⍵}¨files
      todo←files[⍋Order⍳ext]/⍨(ext∊Order)[⍋Order⍳ext]
      ⍝ A few passes, so a file that needs another one (a class needing its
      ⍝ interface, say) loads once its dependency has.
      :For pass :In ⍳3
          failed←⍬
          :For f :In todo
              :Trap 0
                  {}(1+(⊂3⊃⎕NPARTS f)∊'.aplf' '.aplo')ns.⎕FIX'file://',f
              :Else
                  failed,←⊂f
              :EndTrap
          :EndFor
          :If 0=≢todo←failed ⋄ :Leave ⋄ :EndIf
      :EndFor
      warn←{'warning: could not load ',⍵}¨todo
      ⍝ .apla files become variables named after the file (Grid.apla → Grid)
      :For f :In files/⍨ext∊⊂'.apla'
          :Trap 0
              ns.⍙v←ReadApla f
              ns⍎(2⊃⎕NPARTS f),'←⍙v'
          :Else
              warn,←⊂'warning: could not read ',f
          :EndTrap
      :EndFor
    ∇

    ∇ files←FindTests path
    ⍝ path is a test file, or a folder searched recursively.
      :If ~⎕NEXISTS path
          ('No such file or folder: ',path)⎕SIGNAL 22
      :EndIf
      :If 2=1 ⎕NINFO path
          files←,⊂path
      :Else
          files←{⍵[⍋⍵]}Walk(-'/'=⊃⌽path)↓path
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ∇ r←Walk dir;names;types;base;keep
      (names types)←0 1(⎕NINFO⍠1)dir,'/*'
      :If 0=≢names ⋄ r←⍬ ⋄ :Return ⋄ :EndIf
      base←{⌽(∧\'/'≠⌽⍵)/⌽⍵}¨names        ⍝ last part of each path
      keep←~(base∊Skip)∨'.'=⊃¨base       ⍝ skip hidden folders and Skip list
      r←(keep∧(types=2)∧{'_test.aplf'≡¯10↑⍵}¨names)/names
      ⍝ Only recurse when there are subfolders: Walk¨⍬ would still call Walk
      ⍝ once on a blank "prototype" argument.
      :If ∨/keep∧types=1
          r,←⊃,/Walk¨(keep∧types=1)/names
      :EndIf
    ∇

    Folder←{⊃1⎕NPARTS ⍵}
    ⍝ Tests in a tests/ folder test the code in the folder above it
    CodeFolder←{f←Folder ⍵ ⋄ 'tests/'≡¯6↑f:Folder ¯1↓f ⋄ f}

    ∇ a←ReadApla file;lines;NoComment
    ⍝ Array notation file: drop comments and blank lines, join with ⋄, evaluate
      NoComment←{(∧\~(⍵='⍝')>≠\⍵='''')/⍵}
      lines←NoComment¨⊃⎕NGET file 1
      a←⍎¯3↓∊((∨/¨' '≠lines)/lines),¨⊂' ⋄ '
    ∇

    ∇ t←ErrorText dummy;dm
      dm←⎕DMX.DM
      t←⎕DMX.EM,((×≢⎕DMX.Message)/': ',⎕DMX.Message)
      :If 1<≢dm ⋄ t,←'  at ',{⍵/⍨∨\' '≠⍵}2⊃dm ⋄ :EndIf
    ∇

    ∇ Report r;status;name;msgs;n;m
      (status name msgs n)←r
      ⎕←'  ',((('pass' 'fail' 'error')⍳⊂status)⊃'✅' '❌' '💥'),' ',name,(status≡'pass')/'  (',(⍕n),' checks)'
      :For m :In msgs ⋄ ⎕←'       ',m ⋄ :EndFor
    ∇

⍝ ─── Assertions. Copied into each test's namespace, so tests call them
⍝     without a prefix. Failures are collected; the test keeps running.
⍝     Each returns a shy result, 1 (passed) or 0, so they also work as the
⍝     last line of a dfn test, and in conditions: :If 5 ExpectEq x …

    ∇ {ok}←expected ExpectEq actual;e;a;Shape
      ⍙checks+←1
      :If ~ok←expected≡actual
          (e a)←⍙Show¨expected actual
          :If e≡a      ⍝ look the same: say how they differ
              Shape←{0=≢⍴⍵:'⍬ (scalar)' ⋄ ⍕⍴⍵}
              a,←'  (shape ',(Shape expected),' vs ',(Shape actual),', depth ',(⍕≡expected),' vs ',(⍕≡actual),')'
          :EndIf
          Fail'expected ',e,', got ',a
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ∇ {ok}←ExpectTrue b
      ⍙checks+←1
      :If ~ok←(0<≢,b)∧∧/,b≡¨1
          Fail'expected true (1), got ',⍙Show b
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ∇ {ok}←ExpectFalse b
      ⍙checks+←1
      :If ~ok←(0<≢,b)∧∧/,b≡¨0
          Fail'expected false (0), got ',⍙Show b
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ∇ {ok}←expected ExpectNear actual;tol
    ⍝ Numbers equal to within 1e¯6, for floating-point results:
    ⍝   3.14159265 ExpectNear ○1
      ⍙checks+←1
      tol←1e¯6
      :If ~ok←((⍴expected)≡⍴actual)∧∧/,tol≥|expected-actual
          Fail'expected ',(⍙Show expected),' (±',(⍕tol),'), got ',⍙Show actual
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ∇ {ok}←{errnum}ExpectError expr;⍙r
    ⍝ expr (text) must raise an error; errnum 0 (default) means any error.
    ⍝ Common numbers: 2 SYNTAX, 3 INDEX, 4 RANK, 5 LENGTH, 6 VALUE, 11 DOMAIN
      ⍙checks+←1
      :If 0=⎕NC'errnum' ⋄ errnum←0 ⋄ :EndIf
      ok←0
      :Trap 0
          ⍙r←⍎expr
          Fail'expected an error from: ',expr
      :Else
          ok←(errnum=0)∨errnum=⎕EN
          :If ~ok
              Fail'expected error ',(⍕errnum),' from: ',expr,', got ',⎕DMX.EM
          :EndIf
      :EndTrap
    ∇

    ∇ {ok}←Fail msg
    ⍝ Record a failure (call it directly for custom checks)
      ok←0
      ⍙fails,←⊂⍙Where,msg
    ∇

    ∇ w←⍙Where;k
    ⍝ "Test_name[line]: " of the first caller that isn't an assertion
      k←⊃⍸~⎕SI∊'ExpectEq' 'ExpectTrue' 'ExpectFalse' 'ExpectNear' 'ExpectError' 'Fail' '⍙Where' '⍙Show'
      w←''
      :If k≠0 ⋄ w←(k⊃⎕SI),'[',(⍕k⊃⎕LC),']: ' ⋄ :EndIf
    ∇

    ∇ s←⍙Show a
    ⍝ Short, unambiguous text for an array
      :If (0=10|⎕DR a)∧1≥|≡a              ⍝ text: quote it
          s←'''',(,a),''''
      :ElseIf 0=≢a
          s←'⍬'
      :ElseIf 2>≢⍴a
          s←⍕a
      :Else                               ⍝ matrix: rows separated by ⋄
          s←'[',(¯3↓∊({⍵/⍨⌽∨\⌽' '≠⍵}¨↓⍕a),¨⊂' ⋄ '),']'
      :EndIf
      s←{200<≢⍵:(197↑⍵),'...' ⋄ ⍵}s
    ∇
:EndNamespace
